<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Garfield Peak (south slopes to the Garfield-Applegate saddle)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:312-3: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="42.896827" lon="-122.133714"><ele>1973.4</ele><name>Park Headquarters parking</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:crater-lake-park-headquarters (OSM way 208653507); confidence: high; pdf_page: 313; book_elev_ft: 6475; quote: From the parking area at Park Headquarters (6,475 feet) ski east 1.7 miles to the trail's high point</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.880130" lon="-122.116930"><ele>2069.4</ele><name>Sun Notch Trail high point (East Rim Drive)</name><desc>source: OSM East Rim Drive node 40187236, start of the DEM high stretch (6,788 ft, 1.78-1.94 mi from the pin); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 314; book_elev_ft: 6806; quote: Ski east on the Sun Notch Trail 1.7 miles to its high point at 6,806 feet. Here, leave the road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.889000" lon="-122.114000"><ele>2172.1</ele><name>East bend in the forest</name><desc>source: map 75's dots bend east; DEM grade under 15% from the road; confidence: low; pdf_page: 312; quote: map 75: dotted route from 6806' bends east, then curves NW toward the rim</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.891000" lon="-122.116000"><ele>2191.0</ele><name>Gap in the 7,250 ft step</name><desc>source: DEM grid: the step at 42.8915 is 0-12% here, 35-60% further east; confidence: low; pdf_page: 312; quote: map 75: dotted route from 6806' bends east, then curves NW toward the rim</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.895000" lon="-122.115200"><ele>2252.7</ele><name>Parklands</name><desc>source: DEM grid: 5-21% grades; confidence: low; pdf_page: 312; quote: map 75: dotted route from 6806' bends east, then curves NW toward the rim</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.898500" lon="-122.114000"><ele>2322.7</ele><name>Meadows below the saddle</name><desc>source: DEM grid: 12-19% grades; confidence: low; pdf_page: 312; quote: map 75: dotted route from 6806' bends east, then curves NW toward the rim</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.899400" lon="-122.112000"><ele>2360.7</ele><name>Saddle between Garfield and Applegate peaks (eastern dip)</name><desc>source: DEM: rim crest dip at about 7,745 ft, the book's 7,750; the western dip (42.9013,-122.1176) is about 7,710; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 314; book_elev_ft: 7750; quote: climb through forest, then parklands, and finally open meadows to the 7,750-foot caldera rim at the lower saddle between Garfield Peak and Applegate Peak</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Garfield Peak (south slopes to the Garfield-Applegate saddle)</name><desc>1. Park Headquarters parking -&gt; Sun Notch Trail high point (East Rim Drive): osm (high), 1.81 mi | 2. Sun Notch Trail high point (East Rim Drive) -&gt; East bend in the forest: straight (low), 0.63 mi | 3. East bend in the forest -&gt; Gap in the 7,250 ft step: straight (low), 0.17 mi | 4. Gap in the 7,250 ft step -&gt; Parklands: straight (low), 0.28 mi | 5. Parklands -&gt; Meadows below the saddle: straight (low), 0.25 mi | 6. Meadows below the saddle -&gt; Saddle between Garfield and Applegate peaks (eastern dip): straight (low), 0.12 mi</desc>
